{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And you shall keep His charge</b> — to fear Him, that you should guard against sinning before Him. For after He commands in love, He commands in fear, and He commands in statutes and in judgments and in commandments. Or: 'and you shall keep His charge' — that you should keep that which HaShem keeps, for He keeps the strangers and shows favor to the poor and needy and executes justice for the orphan and widow, in the manner stated elsewhere (I Kings 2:3), 'to keep the charge of YHWH your Elohim, to walk in His ways,' and they said (Shabbat 133a): Just as He is gracious and compassionate, so too you be gracious and compassionate, etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The verse citation מלכים א ב ג resolved to I Kings 2:3."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:14:01.803530366Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}